1
00:00:00,405 --> 00:00:03,080
Anthropic just lost $80.7 billion.

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,311
In six months.

3
00:00:04,666 --> 00:00:08,194
And yet, investors want to value it at up to $2
trillion.

4
00:00:08,544 --> 00:00:10,833
One of these numbers is mostly an illusion.

5
00:00:10,833 --> 00:00:14,079
And the number that could really sink it isn’t
on screen yet.

6
00:00:15,273 --> 00:00:17,405
First: how strong is Anthropic, really?

7
00:00:17,753 --> 00:00:22,878
At the start of 2025, its revenue was running at
about $1 billion a year.

8
00:00:23,078 --> 00:00:25,996
By July 2026: $65 billion.

9
00:00:26,312 --> 00:00:29,771
Its CEO said they planned for 10x growth, and
got 80x.

10
00:00:30,071 --> 00:00:33,565
That’s ahead of OpenAI, reportedly at around $40
billion.

11
00:00:33,915 --> 00:00:42,946
One survey, by Menlo Ventures, an Anthropic
investor, gave it 40% of enterprise AI-model
spending, and 54% of coding.

12
00:00:43,333 --> 00:00:46,083
Amazon put in about $13 billion.

13
00:00:46,233 --> 00:00:49,397
That stake is now marked at roughly $190
billion.

14
00:00:49,785 --> 00:00:50,535
Its valuation?

15
00:00:50,535 --> 00:00:53,911
$61.5 billion in March 2025.

16
00:00:54,178 --> 00:00:57,128
$965 billion this May.

17
00:00:57,128 --> 00:00:59,363
Now, IPO talk of up to $2 trillion.

18
00:01:01,091 --> 00:01:05,241
Then the draft IPO filing leaked, with three
numbers that stunned Wall Street.

19
00:01:05,541 --> 00:01:09,795
Revenue, first half of 2026: $16.3 billion.

20
00:01:10,095 --> 00:01:12,157
Net loss: $80.7 billion.

21
00:01:12,557 --> 00:01:17,570
Cash and short-term investments, end of 2025:
$20.28 billion.

22
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,150
That loss is $13.5 billion a month.

23
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,303
At that rate, twenty billion lasts about 45
days.

24
00:01:24,644 --> 00:01:25,969
Dead by Valentine’s Day.

25
00:01:26,119 --> 00:01:26,469
So…

26
00:01:26,619 --> 00:01:27,188
why isn’t it?

27
00:01:29,455 --> 00:01:32,846
Because about $72 billion of that loss never
left the building.

28
00:01:33,146 --> 00:01:35,921
It’s an accounting charge on convertible notes:

29
00:01:35,921 --> 00:01:38,874
money investors lent that turns into shares
later.

30
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:39,864
Picture it:

31
00:01:39,864 --> 00:01:45,219
a friend lends you $10, and you promise to repay
in your company’s shares, at today’s price.

32
00:01:45,501 --> 00:01:47,676
Your company becomes ten times more valuable.

33
00:01:47,676 --> 00:01:50,328
Those shares are now worth $100.

34
00:01:50,601 --> 00:01:52,551
On paper, you just lost $90.

35
00:01:52,551 --> 00:01:54,322
In cash, you spent nothing.

36
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:59,181
Anthropic’s valuation jumped about two and a
half times in three months.

37
00:01:59,181 --> 00:02:02,441
The notes got pricier, and the reported loss
exploded.

38
00:02:02,831 --> 00:02:06,032
The stronger Anthropic gets, the more money it
appears to lose.

39
00:02:06,482 --> 00:02:12,640
The proof: that same quarter, Amazon marked
those very notes up by $55.7 billion.

40
00:02:12,990 --> 00:02:16,877
Strip the charge out, and the $80 billion loss
shrinks to under $9 billion.

41
00:02:17,277 --> 00:02:18,310
So the loss is fake?

42
00:02:19,672 --> 00:02:20,397
Not so fast.

43
00:02:20,397 --> 00:02:23,197
There’s a number in the filing that is very,
very real.

44
00:02:23,562 --> 00:02:24,312
Compute.

45
00:02:24,487 --> 00:02:29,078
Its half-year compute bill went from $2.3
billion to nearly $9 billion.

46
00:02:29,396 --> 00:02:36,819
And the filing reportedly lists at least $518
billion in AI-infrastructure commitments over
roughly a decade.

47
00:02:37,107 --> 00:02:37,557
Google.

48
00:02:37,682 --> 00:02:38,307
Amazon.

49
00:02:38,432 --> 00:02:39,057
Microsoft.

50
00:02:39,232 --> 00:02:40,107
Nvidia chips.

51
00:02:40,257 --> 00:02:41,457
Broadcom-linked leases.

52
00:02:41,774 --> 00:02:43,915
About 80% of it can’t be cancelled.

53
00:02:44,362 --> 00:02:46,037
Now put the cash next to it.

54
00:02:46,037 --> 00:02:47,952
The bill is about 25 times bigger.

55
00:02:48,459 --> 00:02:53,829
Yes, that cash figure is from December, and $95
billion in new funding has been announced since.

56
00:02:53,829 --> 00:02:56,182
Still a fraction of the bill.

57
00:02:56,538 --> 00:03:02,261
Its compute landlords are also its investors,
and, the filing warns, increasingly its rivals.

58
00:03:02,561 --> 00:03:06,360
And roughly a fifth to a quarter of revenue
comes from just two customers.

59
00:03:07,636 --> 00:03:13,848
So: strong, or fragile? Valuations range from
$144 billion to $2 trillion.

60
00:03:14,198 --> 00:03:15,618
Look at those three numbers again.

61
00:03:15,868 --> 00:03:18,840
$16.3 billion in revenue: real demand.

62
00:03:19,140 --> 00:03:23,088
$80.7 billion in losses: mostly the price of
success.

63
00:03:23,388 --> 00:03:27,023
$20.28 billion in cash: a snapshot, not a
runway.

64
00:03:27,504 --> 00:03:29,129
That’s why it’s going public.

65
00:03:29,129 --> 00:03:31,246
It needs the deepest pool of capital on Earth.

66
00:03:31,657 --> 00:03:37,052
Anthropic’s strength is real. So is the bill.
The only question is which one grows faster.

67
00:03:37,852 --> 00:03:40,182
For more on the money behind AI, subscribe.
